        "id": 1958755
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-08T16:38:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we still need to use `btm_ble_stop_observe()` because this is the only way that we make scanning activity to be none. `btm_ble_stop_scan()` only disables scanning but activity is still on; that is, `is_ble_scan_active() \u003d\u003d true`. This will makes us not go into `if (!btm_cb.ble_ctr_cb.is_ble_scan_active())` statement to reset scanning parameters to be low latency.\n\nIn my local test, if we only do `btm_ble_stop_scan()`, we still not set scanning parameters as low latency since`is_ble_scan_active()` is still true.\n\nplease correct me if I misunderstand something, thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "eca35d72_66f09150",
      "revId": "9a59494adb8c88ec5bcaa7719b59ac1c69705452",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
